1
00:05:16,666 --> 00:05:22,666
Believing is Everything

2
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:39,333
Over the Moon is a animation, adventure, family film directed by Glen Keane.

3
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Fueled by memories of her mother, resourceful Fei Fei builds a rocket to the moon
on a mission to prove the existence of a legendary moon goddess.

4
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
Fei Fei (voice), played by Cathy Ang.

5
00:26:23,333 --> 00:26:29,333
Chang'e (voice), played by Phillipa Soo.

6
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Chin (voice), played by Robert G. Chiu.

7
00:36:56,666 --> 00:37:02,666
Gobi (voice), played by Ken Jeong.

8
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
Father (voice), played by John Cho.

9
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Mrs. Zhong (voice), played by Sandra Oh.

10
00:52:46,666 --> 00:52:52,666
Over the Moon is a 2020 animated musical fantasy film directed by Glen Keane (in his feature directorial debut) and co-directed by John
Kahrs, from a screenplay by Audrey Wells, with additional screenplay material by Alice Wu and Jennifer Yee McDevitt.

11
00:58:03,333 --> 00:58:09,333
The film was produced by Pearl Studio and Netflix Animation,
and animated by Sony Pictures Imageworks.

12
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
It stars the voices of Cathy Ang, Phillipa Soo, Ken Jeong, John
Cho, Ruthie Ann Miles, Margaret Cho, and Sandra Oh.

13
01:08:36,666 --> 01:08:42,666
The plot follows an adventurous girl named Fei Fei, who builds a rocket
ship to meet the mythical goddess on the Moon Chang'e.

14
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
Over the Moon was first shown at the Montclair Film Festival on October 17, 2020,
followed by its Netflix and select theaters release on October 23.

15
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:16,000
The film grossed $860,000 worldwide; it earned a Golden Globe nomination for Best Animated
Feature Film, and was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 93rd Academy Awards.

16
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
It is the final film Wells worked on before her
death and was dedicated to her memory.

17
01:29:43,333 --> 01:29:49,333
The film explores themes of moon, musical, rocket, approving.
